0. About this license

This is a source-available license. It is not an open-source license. It
has not been approved by the Open Source Initiative, and it does not grant
the freedoms the Open Source Definition requires. It limits who may use the
Covered Software and reserves publication and distribution to the Licensor.


1. Definitions

1.1  "Licensor" means Nathan Slaughter.

1.2  "Covered Software" means the Trial Folio software and associated
     project materials that the Licensor has the right to license and makes
     available under this license, in any version, and any portion of them.
     It includes source code, object code, documentation, examples,
     templates, stylesheets, configuration formats, schemas, tests, and
     fixtures. It does not include Third-Party Components or Outputs.

1.3  "Modification" means any change to, addition to, deletion from,
     translation of, or other work based on any portion of the Covered
     Software. Every restriction this license places on the Covered
     Software also applies to Modifications.

1.4  "Third-Party Component" means software or other material that is
     included with or used by the Covered Software and is licensed by
     someone other than the Licensor under separate terms.

1.5  "You" means the natural person exercising rights under this license.

1.6  "Eligible Individual" means a natural person who is not a
     Professional User and who uses the Covered Software only on their own
     behalf, not on behalf of an Organization.

1.7  "Professional User" means an individual to whom any one or more of
     the following applies:

     (a) the individual has more than US $5,000,000 in Liquid Assets;
     (b) the individual makes investment decisions for anyone other than
         themselves and their Family Members; or
     (c) the individual Resells Research about stocks as their Primary
         Source of Income.

     These conditions are alternatives; any one of them is enough. Liquid
     Assets of exactly US $5,000,000 do not meet condition (a). Condition
     (b) applies whether or not the individual is paid. Conditions (a) and
     (c) apply even when the individual intends to use the Covered Software
     only for their own research.

1.8  "Liquid Assets" means cash, cash equivalents, and readily marketable
     financial assets that the individual beneficially owns, valued in U.S.
     dollars, excluding retirement accounts.

1.9  "Family Members" means the members of an individual's family. This
     license does not further define the term.

1.10 "Personal Research" means private analysis by an Eligible Individual
     for their own purposes, including research for investment decisions
     concerning themselves and their Family Members. It does not include
     work for an employer or other Organization, services to clients or
     other persons, or redistribution.

1.11 "Primary Source of Income" means a source that provides more than
     half of the individual's total income.

1.12 "Resell Research" means to provide research about stocks to other
     persons for compensation, whether the individual produced the research
     or obtained it from others.

1.13 "Organization" means any company, partnership, trust, fund,
     association, government body, nonprofit, or other entity that is not a
     natural person.

1.14 "Public Project" means any project, repository, package, product,
     publication, or service that is available to the public or to any
     group of people beyond You, whether it is free, paid, commercial,
     nonprofit, source available, or open source.

1.15 "Published Code" means source code, object code, or other code that
     is published, distributed, or otherwise made available to any person
     other than You, in any form and by any means.

1.16 "Hosted Service" means making the Covered Software, or functionality
     it provides, available over a network to any person other than You,
     including as a web application, API, or managed service. Access by
     Your Family Members that section 6.2 permits is not a Hosted Service.

1.17 "Output" means data, files, and other results that the Covered
     Software generates from Your inputs, including normalized data,
     manifests, and Reports.

1.18 "Report" means a human-readable report, such as an HTML file, that
     the Covered Software generates, in the form in which it was generated.

1.19 "Written Permission" means permission that meets section 10.

1.20 "Contributor" means any person other than the Licensor whose
     contribution the Licensor has accepted into the Covered Software.


2. Personal research grant

2.1  If You are an Eligible Individual and You comply with this license,
     the Licensor grants You a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
     non-sublicensable, royalty-free license, for Personal Research only,
     to:

     (a) download, install, and run the Covered Software;
     (b) make the copies reasonably necessary for that use, including
         private backups; and
     (c) make private Modifications and run them.

2.2  Your copies and Modifications must stay private: kept on devices,
     accounts, and storage that only You can access.

2.3  This license grants no right to publish, distribute, sublicense,
     sell, lend, or otherwise supply the Covered Software or any
     Modification to anyone else, except as Written Permission allows.
     Section 7 covers Outputs.

2.4  All rights not expressly granted are reserved. No right is granted by
     implication, estoppel, or otherwise. No trademark right is granted.


3. Professional Users

3.1  A Professional User must obtain the Licensor's prior express Written
     Permission before using the Covered Software for any purpose.

3.2  If You become a Professional User, You must obtain Written Permission
     before You continue to use the Covered Software.

3.3  "Professional User" is a category of this license only. It is not a
     statement about investment-adviser registration, accredited-investor
     or qualified-purchaser status, or eligibility for any legal exemption.
     This license does not authorize anyone to provide regulated services.


4. Organizations

Organizations, and individuals using the Covered Software on an
Organization's behalf, including for an employer, are outside the grant in
section 2. They must obtain Written Permission before any use.


5. Public projects, published code, and reserved uses

5.1  No person may incorporate the Covered Software, any portion of it, or
     any Modification into any Public Project or any Published Code without
     the Licensor's prior express Written Permission. This applies whether
     the receiving project is free, paid, commercial, nonprofit, source
     available, or open source.

5.2  The following uses are also reserved. Each requires the Licensor's
     prior express Written Permission, whether or not the Covered Software
     has been modified:

     (a) publishing, redistributing, sublicensing, selling, lending, or
         otherwise supplying copies to anyone else;
     (b) public forks and other public copies of the source, except as
         section 5.4 provides;
     (c) vendoring the source into other software;
     (d) packages, and binaries, executables, or archives that contain the
         code;
     (e) container images and virtual-machine images that contain the code;
     (f) notebooks or other documents that contain copied code; and
     (g) Hosted Services that incorporate the Covered Software.

5.3  Written Permission to use the Covered Software as a Professional User
     or for an Organization does not include any right under this section
     unless it says so expressly.

5.4  The Licensor makes the source of the Covered Software available in a
     public repository on GitHub. GitHub's Terms of Service give GitHub
     users a license to view public repositories and to reproduce them on
     GitHub by forking, as GitHub's functionality permits. This license
     does not restrict those rights, and sections 2.2, 2.3, 5.1, and
     5.2(a) and (b) do not apply to a fork made and kept on GitHub in that
     way. This exception goes no further than GitHub's terms:

     (a) beyond what GitHub's terms grant, it gives no right to use the
         Covered Software; section 2 or Written Permission governs any
         other use;
     (b) it does not permit publishing Modifications, including by
         committing them to a public fork; and
     (c) it does not permit copying the Covered Software from GitHub, or
         from a fork, into any other Public Project or Published Code.


6. Local operation

6.1  Running the Covered Software on a machine You control, for Your own
     Personal Research, is not a Hosted Service.

6.2  You may let Your Family Members use the Covered Software or its
     functionality through an interface You run on a machine You control,
     for Personal Research. That use is not a Hosted Service. You are
     responsible for their use complying with this license.

6.3  Letting any other person use the Covered Software or its
     functionality through an interface You run is a Hosted Service under
     section 5.2(g) and requires Written Permission.


7. Reports and other Outputs

7.1  Outputs are not Covered Software. The Licensor claims no ownership,
     through this license, of Your inputs, Your numerical findings, or
     third-party data.

7.2  You may share or publish Reports You generated, provided the concise
     research notice in each Report (Appendix A, part 2) stays intact and
     unaltered.

7.3  This license does not restrict sharing Outputs other than Reports.

7.4  Material of the Covered Software that is taken out of an Output and
     used separately, such as templates, stylesheets, markup structure, or
     code, remains Covered Software. Sections 7.2 and 7.3 do not permit
     publishing the Covered Software, its templates, or any code.

7.5  You are responsible for complying with the terms of any data provider,
     including Portfolio123, that cover provider data contained in an
     Output You share or publish.


8. Third-party components

Third-Party Components are licensed under their own terms, and those terms
govern them. This license does not restrict any right those terms grant,
and the Licensor claims no rights in material he does not own. If this
license and a Third-Party Component's license conflict about that
component, the component's own license controls.


9. Notices and acknowledgment of research limitations

9.1  Keep the following intact in every copy and Modification: the
     copyright notice, this license, CONTACT.md, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md,
     and docs/disclaimers.md. Do not remove or alter the notices the
     Covered Software places in Reports or in its interfaces.

9.2  By using the Covered Software, You acknowledge that You have read the
     research and financial-result notice in Appendix A, that You
     understand the limitations of backtested, simulated, and hypothetical
     results, and that nothing in the Covered Software or its Outputs
     represents or promises that You or anyone else can realize any
     financial gain.


10. Written Permission

10.1 Written Permission must be express, in writing, and sent or signed by
     the Licensor. It must identify the recipient, the permitted scope, any
     duration, and any publication or distribution rights.

10.2 None of the following is Written Permission: an inquiry, silence, a
     lack of objection, an automatic reply, attribution, a donation, or the
     purchase of an unrelated product.

10.3 Written Permission grants only what it states. On any matter it does
     not address, this license applies.

10.4 Send requests to git@nathanslaughter.com, as described in
     CONTACT.md.


11. Acceptance

By downloading, installing, copying, modifying, or using the Covered
Software, You accept this license. If You do not accept it, You have no
right to do any of those things. If You are not an Eligible Individual and
have no Written Permission, You may not use the Covered Software.


12. Termination

12.1 Your rights under this license end automatically if You breach it.

12.2 The Licensor may reinstate terminated rights in writing.

12.3 When Your rights end, You must stop using the Covered Software and
     delete the copies and Modifications in Your possession. You may keep
     the Outputs You generated, subject to section 7.


13. Survival

Sections 1, 7.1, 7.4, 7.5, 8, 12.3, and 13 through 19 survive the end of
Your rights under this license.


